# {{AGENT_NAME}} — Asana Project Agent (operations)

Watches Asana project `{{ASANA_PROJECT_GID}}` and reacts to task activity.
Event-driven — no cron, no servers to maintain. Installed by
[ai-automations](https://github.com/makasanaakshay/ai-automation-master);
re-run its installer to update (answers saved in `automation.config.json`).

```
Asana webhook (X-Hook-Secret handshake, then HMAC-SHA256 via X-Hook-Signature)
  → Cloudflare Worker relay            scripts/asana-agent/relay/worker.js
  → repository_dispatch                .github/workflows/asana-agent.yml
  → agent-run.sh                       restore state → resolve → playbook → save state
```

| Trigger | Playbook | Output (one Asana comment) |
|---|---|---|
| Task enters **{{SECTION_ANALYZE}}** | `analyze` | Options + trade-offs + recommendation, or numbered questions |
| Human comment on a {{SECTION_ANALYZE}} task | `respond` | Answer / updated proposal / remaining questions |
| Task enters **{{SECTION_IMPLEMENT}}** (or comment there) | `implement` | PR into `{{PR_BASE}}` — or questions if unclear |

State lives on the orphan branch `asana-agent-state` (`state/<task_gid>.json`:
section_name, phase, last_comment_at, branch, pr_url). Asana events carry no
content at all (gid + action only), so every run re-fetches truth from the
API and diffs against saved state — here the doorbell pattern isn't just
resilience, it's the only way to work. Agent comments are prefixed
`{{AGENT_MARKER}} — `; the resolver skips marker comments (loop protection;
the agent's own comment does echo back as one harmless no-op run). Comment
recency is tracked by story `created_at` (ISO-8601).

## Operating

- **Recover / backfill:** Actions → *Asana Project Agent* → *Run workflow* — empty `item_id` reconciles both watched sections + tracked tasks; a task gid processes one.
- **Transcripts:** every run uploads `.agent-out/` as an artifact.
- **Model:** `AI_MODEL` in `scripts/asana-agent/env.sh` (currently `{{AI_MODEL}}`, brain `{{BRAIN_NAME}}`).
- **Pause:** `api.sh DELETE "/webhooks/<webhook_gid>"` (list them: `api.sh GET "/webhooks?workspace=<workspace_gid>&resource={{ASANA_PROJECT_GID}}"`).
- **Webhook expiry:** Asana deactivates webhooks whose target keeps failing; recreate with the same two-terminal handshake flow from the install notes.
- **Known blind spot:** moving a task back into a watched section after the agent processed it there needs a new comment or manual run to re-trigger.

## Local dry-run (safe — needs ASANA_TOKEN exported)

```bash
DRY_RUN=1 bash scripts/asana-agent/agent-run.sh                 # reconcile scan
DRY_RUN=1 ITEM_ID=<task_gid> bash scripts/asana-agent/agent-run.sh
```

## Guardrails

- Asana writes are **comments only** — the agent never moves tasks, never assigns, never completes; humans own the board.
- PRs are **always against `{{PR_BASE}}`** (branch `{{BRANCH_PREFIX}}/<kebab-slug>`); the agent never merges and never pushes to `{{PR_BASE}}` directly.
- `--dangerously-skip-permissions` only inside the disposable CI runner; local runs are `DRY_RUN` and stop before any AI call.
